                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 2 at 10:56PM ChST until October 5 at 4:00AM ChST by NWS Tiyan GU",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Guam, Rota, Tinian, and Saipan.\n\n* WHEN...Through late Sunday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Tropical Storm Choi-wan (26W) is nearly stationary and is\nexpected to pivot north-northeast through the northern CNMI\nthrough the weekend near Pagan and Agrihan. To the south of\nChoi-wan, surging monsoon inflow will maintain wet conditions\ninto early next week, resulting in 4 to 6 inches of rain for Guam\nand Rota, and 5 to 8 inches for Tinian and Saipan during the\nWatch period.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
